    "id": "ACT-GRAM",
    "revision": 6,
    "title": "Extend 把 to brief actions and object relations",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk5-ba-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Extend 把 to brief actions and object relations",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "After 把 and an identifiable object, 一 + verb can present one brief action before what follows. A different frame puts a second related object after the verb: 把 X 当作 Y says that X is treated as Y. The verb must support the stated relation; two unrelated objects cannot simply be added.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他把书一放，就走了。",
                "pinyin": "tā bǎ shū yī fàng ， jiù zǒu le 。",
                "meaning": "He set down the book and left.",
                "audio": "bb06ca4c9da5e193d87ff9edd9571d6820846178f5afa69b5c90bf131a37da2e"
              },
              {
                "text": "他把点头当作同意。",
                "pinyin": "tā bǎ diǎntóu dàngzuò tóngyì 。",
                "meaning": "He treated a nod as agreement.",
                "audio": "5e3e80db67a2277bc33eb421176ce6bcaac47b295c8c978d3f36e2d063ab60f3"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
